1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,500
[laughing]

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,166
Up, up! Up, up!

3
00:00:06,166 --> 00:00:07,708
[barking]

4
00:00:07,708 --> 00:00:10,208
[laughing playfully]

5
00:00:11,875 --> 00:00:12,958
Go get it!

6
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:13,958
Whoa!

7
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:15,416
[laughing]

8
00:00:15,416 --> 00:00:17,166
-[dog growling]
-What is it, boy?

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,916
[growling and barking]

10
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:23,458
Hey!

11
00:00:23,458 --> 00:00:24,916
I think you dropped your doll.

12
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:30,208
Well, hello there!

13
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:31,833
Hi, I'm Arin!

14
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:35,000
Ah, I wasn't supposed
to tell anyone my name.

15
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,666
Hmm, why not?

16
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:40,458
My, uh, teacher told me
not to tell strangers who I am,

17
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:41,458
ever.

18
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,708
Well, Arin, I'm Koji,

19
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:45,000
and that's Aru and Ume.

20
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Hi!

21
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,166
So now we're not strangers.

22
00:00:48,166 --> 00:00:49,666
[chuckling warmly]
How can we help you?

23
00:00:49,666 --> 00:00:51,833
Well, I could use some food,

24
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:53,333
and maybe some water.

25
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,000
Of course,
I'm willing to work for it!

26
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,500
Anything around here
you need help with?

27
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,791
I know how to water plants,

28
00:00:57,791 --> 00:00:59,625
fold laundry, make pies,

29
00:00:59,625 --> 00:01:00,750
whatever...

30
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:03,041
[chuckling]
We can figure that out later.

31
00:01:03,041 --> 00:01:04,375
First things first.

32
00:01:04,375 --> 00:01:05,541
Join us for dinner.

33
00:01:05,541 --> 00:01:06,500
[laughing] Yeah!

34
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:07,500
Thanks.

35
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,333
[dog barking]

36
00:01:14,708 --> 00:01:18,083
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

37
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:20,916
♪ Together we will rise ♪

38
00:01:20,916 --> 00:01:24,375
♪ We fight ♪

39
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:27,250
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

40
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:32,250
[screaming]

41
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:35,375
[scream turns into laughter]

42
00:01:35,375 --> 00:01:37,125
[laughing] Oh, wow,

43
00:01:37,125 --> 00:01:40,083
that Lobbo guy
sounds like a laugh riot.

44
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:41,333
"Lobbo Lobbo!"

45
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:44,833
[laughing]

46
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:45,833
[sighing]

47
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:47,083
Thank you so much

48
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:48,875
for everything.

49
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:49,916
[Aru] Thanks.

50
00:01:49,916 --> 00:01:52,083
Uh, I can't take this.

51
00:01:52,083 --> 00:01:53,250
Please!

52
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:56,291
You need someone
to protect you out there.

53
00:01:56,291 --> 00:01:58,625
Maybe I do.

54
00:01:58,625 --> 00:01:59,458
Thanks again.

55
00:01:59,458 --> 00:02:01,125
Come back anytime.

56
00:02:01,125 --> 00:02:02,583
Lobbo Lobbo.

57
00:02:02,583 --> 00:02:04,333
[laughing]

58
00:02:12,291 --> 00:02:14,000
[sighing]

59
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:32,416
I'm back.

60
00:02:32,416 --> 00:02:33,500
[growling]

61
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,666
[Ras] You were gone too long.

62
00:02:35,666 --> 00:02:38,500
Did you bring food?

63
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,875
I did.

64
00:02:42,041 --> 00:02:43,916
[grumbling] Mm...

65
00:02:43,916 --> 00:02:45,625
Did you steal this?

66
00:02:45,625 --> 00:02:47,250
Here it comes. Nrrr...

67
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,416
Here comes the bounty.

68
00:02:48,416 --> 00:02:49,583
[Ras grunting] Mm-mm.

69
00:02:49,583 --> 00:02:51,541
Nrr...oom!

70
00:02:51,541 --> 00:02:53,958
Or have to
attack the villagers for it?

71
00:02:53,958 --> 00:02:55,375
I just said the magic word.

72
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:57,458
You know incantations?

73
00:02:57,458 --> 00:02:59,750
[chewing] Mm... mm...

74
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:01,833
I said "please."

75
00:03:01,833 --> 00:03:03,000
Some people just want to help.

76
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,041
[chomping] Mm...

77
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:07,208
You can't depend on help.

78
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:08,958
If you want true power,

79
00:03:08,958 --> 00:03:10,958
you need to take things
by force.

80
00:03:10,958 --> 00:03:14,291
People always act
in their own self interest.

81
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:15,708
Put that away!

82
00:03:15,708 --> 00:03:17,625
It's time to focus
on your training.

83
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:18,583
Get up.

84
00:03:18,583 --> 00:03:20,500
[gulping] I--

85
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,875
[growling]

86
00:03:22,791 --> 00:03:23,708
Of course.

87
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,625
Your form is sloppy.

88
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:32,083
Shoulders back.

89
00:03:32,083 --> 00:03:33,416
Lower your center.

90
00:03:33,416 --> 00:03:34,375
[grumbling]

91
00:03:34,375 --> 00:03:35,875
[grunting with effort]

92
00:03:42,666 --> 00:03:43,791
Whoa! [grunting]

93
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,125
Weeks of training,

94
00:03:48,125 --> 00:03:50,083
and you're still not improving.

95
00:03:50,083 --> 00:03:52,666
I thought I was.

96
00:03:52,666 --> 00:03:56,083
I can see the doubt
on your face.

97
00:03:56,083 --> 00:03:59,041
Push through your weakness.

98
00:03:59,041 --> 00:04:01,916
Focus on your strength,

99
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:03,875
on your anger.

100
00:04:03,875 --> 00:04:08,166
Turn your hurt into power.

101
00:04:08,166 --> 00:04:09,500
But that's not how the Ninja--

102
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,625
The Ninja are no longer
your teachers!

103
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:14,125
[gasping and wheezing]

104
00:04:17,291 --> 00:04:22,041
Ah... yes, there it is.

105
00:04:22,041 --> 00:04:25,250
<i>I need to know,</i>
<i>did you cause the Merge?</i>

106
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:27,916
<i>Yes...</i>

107
00:04:27,916 --> 00:04:29,625
<i>[screaming]</i>

108
00:04:29,625 --> 00:04:30,708
<i>Arin!</i>

109
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:31,791
<i>[screaming] No!</i>

110
00:04:31,791 --> 00:04:33,250
[screaming]

111
00:04:36,916 --> 00:04:37,791
[gasping]

112
00:04:39,125 --> 00:04:40,416
[Ras grumbling] Mm...

113
00:04:40,416 --> 00:04:43,375
Never doubt my teachings.

114
00:04:49,666 --> 00:04:52,083
[sniffing]

115
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,416
[whining sadly]

116
00:04:53,416 --> 00:04:55,625
[sighing]
Riyu's lost Arin's scent.

117
00:04:55,625 --> 00:04:58,875
Well, Arin
had to have come this way,

118
00:04:58,875 --> 00:05:00,375
so let's keep on this path.

119
00:05:00,375 --> 00:05:01,333
[sniffing]

120
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:02,916
[whining]

121
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:07,083
[Lloyd] Okay,
didn't see this coming.

122
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:08,291
Why didn't Arin leave

123
00:05:08,291 --> 00:05:10,250
like a trail of pie crumbs
or something

124
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,458
so we could follow him?

125
00:05:11,458 --> 00:05:14,083
Because I'm not sure
he wants to be followed.

126
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:16,125
[sniffing]

127
00:05:19,375 --> 00:05:21,375
[whining]

128
00:05:23,666 --> 00:05:26,333
You ask me,
the cave seems way more likely.

129
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:28,666
That other way is super rocky
and dangerous.

130
00:05:28,666 --> 00:05:30,208
My thoughts as well,

131
00:05:30,208 --> 00:05:33,208
but the cave is too small
for Zanth to enter.

132
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:35,041
I can take her
down the mountain

133
00:05:35,041 --> 00:05:36,291
and search that direction

134
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,083
while you explore the cave.

135
00:05:38,083 --> 00:05:39,041
I don't love the idea

136
00:05:39,041 --> 00:05:40,958
of sending you
down that way alone.

137
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:41,833
[Zanth snorting]

138
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:43,333
[Zane] I will not be alone.

139
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:45,625
It is a good idea
to search both directions.

140
00:05:45,625 --> 00:05:46,958
Just be careful.

141
00:05:46,958 --> 00:05:48,833
"Careful"
would be my middle name

142
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:50,625
if Nindroid naming conventions

143
00:05:50,625 --> 00:05:51,958
allowed for such things,

144
00:05:51,958 --> 00:05:53,250
which they do not.

145
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:54,166
Good luck, Zane.

146
00:05:54,166 --> 00:05:56,041
We'll meet you
on the other side.

147
00:05:56,041 --> 00:05:57,750
Uh, that came out weird.

148
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:59,041
I mean, of the mountain,

149
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:01,000
not meet you
in the Departed Realm.

150
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,833
Does the Departed Realm
still exist after the Merge?

151
00:06:03,833 --> 00:06:06,333
That's actually
a very good question,

152
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:07,500
but I'm hoping

153
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,416
we don't have to find out
anytime soon.

154
00:06:13,958 --> 00:06:15,583
I can see the path ahead.

155
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,541
Follow me! I got this!

156
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,041
[quietly]
Who made this guy boss?

157
00:06:20,041 --> 00:06:22,125
He's just trying to be helpful.

158
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:23,541
Ease up on him a little.

159
00:06:23,541 --> 00:06:24,791
[Sora] What?

160
00:06:24,791 --> 00:06:27,500
I haven't said
anything sarcastic all day.

161
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,666
[Frak] I've got a really great
cave sense.

162
00:06:29,666 --> 00:06:32,333
[mocking] "I've got
a really great cave sense."

163
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:34,791
Okay, so one
sarcastic thing now.

164
00:06:34,791 --> 00:06:36,500
[snorting chuckle]

165
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,083
Us Serpentine are brilliant
at underground spaces.

166
00:06:39,083 --> 00:06:41,208
This is just like
the Ninjago sewers.

167
00:06:41,208 --> 00:06:45,958
Well, except the smell's
a little, uh, different.

168
00:07:05,166 --> 00:07:06,958
[candle tumbling]

169
00:07:06,958 --> 00:07:08,041
[Sora gasping]

170
00:07:08,041 --> 00:07:10,583
Not creepy at all.

171
00:07:12,958 --> 00:07:14,791
Ah... check this out!

172
00:07:14,791 --> 00:07:16,791
It's just like the stuff
I've been studying.

173
00:07:16,791 --> 00:07:18,791
You study cave writing
in your spare time?

174
00:07:18,791 --> 00:07:19,958
Sure.

175
00:07:19,958 --> 00:07:21,666
I'm interested
in all things speleological.

176
00:07:21,666 --> 00:07:22,708
No one has ever said that.

177
00:07:22,708 --> 00:07:24,166
Okay,

178
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:26,375
well, I can't translate these
without my books,

179
00:07:26,375 --> 00:07:27,416
but from what I can tell,

180
00:07:27,416 --> 00:07:29,458
this cave has been used before.

181
00:07:29,458 --> 00:07:30,458
Wow.

182
00:07:30,458 --> 00:07:31,708
You learned all of that

183
00:07:31,708 --> 00:07:33,750
from your spel... obian books?

184
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:35,750
[scoffing]
"Speleology," please.

185
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:37,250
Can we not bicker?

186
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:38,666
Let's go.

187
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,416
Look! There's--

188
00:07:43,416 --> 00:07:44,708
-Another tunnel!
---another tunnel!

189
00:07:45,375 --> 00:07:46,666
Let's go this way.

190
00:07:47,666 --> 00:07:50,500
Uh, this looks tight.

191
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:52,916
If you're worried,
let me lead the way.

192
00:07:52,916 --> 00:07:55,375
Hope no one is claustrophobic.

193
00:07:55,375 --> 00:07:57,416
Huh, probably
should've asked that

194
00:07:57,416 --> 00:07:59,833
before we started.

195
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,208
[grunting]

196
00:08:03,208 --> 00:08:04,333
[gasping]

197
00:08:04,333 --> 00:08:05,500
[Frak] Hey, you okay?

198
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,583
I'm fine.

199
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:08,833
There's a cool
Serpentine trick I use

200
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:10,916
when I start to get
claustrophobic.

201
00:08:10,916 --> 00:08:12,333
I just breathe in
through my nose...

202
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:13,333
[inhaling]

203
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,750
...then hiss it out.

204
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,500
[exhaling, hissing]

205
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,166
[inhaling]

206
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:20,291
[shuddering exhale]

207
00:08:32,041 --> 00:08:33,625
What now, cave man?

208
00:08:33,625 --> 00:08:36,041
Let me just move
some of these rocks.

209
00:08:37,375 --> 00:08:39,458
You sure those aren't, like,

210
00:08:39,458 --> 00:08:41,541
holding up the cave roof
or something?

211
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:44,708
Speleologist here.

212
00:08:44,708 --> 00:08:45,916
[stones rumbling]

213
00:08:45,916 --> 00:08:47,833
But what's that sound?

214
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,125
I don't hear anything.

215
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:50,291
-[stones crumbling]
-It's a cave-in.

216
00:08:50,291 --> 00:08:51,875
I shouldn't've moved
those rocks!

217
00:08:51,875 --> 00:08:53,125
Run!

218
00:08:53,125 --> 00:08:55,291
Uh, oh, but, yay, I was right!

219
00:08:55,291 --> 00:08:56,291
There's a light up ahead!

220
00:08:56,291 --> 00:08:57,875
[rocks crumbling]

221
00:08:57,875 --> 00:09:00,083
We're saved!

222
00:09:02,791 --> 00:09:04,500
We're not saved.

223
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,666
Any ideas?

224
00:09:05,666 --> 00:09:07,583
I can't stop the cave-in
with my quake powers.

225
00:09:07,583 --> 00:09:09,708
It's too big, too fast!

226
00:09:09,708 --> 00:09:12,333
Riyu, can you--?

227
00:09:12,333 --> 00:09:13,416
[screaming]

228
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:17,583
[screaming]

229
00:09:21,458 --> 00:09:22,541
I'm bored.

230
00:09:22,541 --> 00:09:25,041
This is boring!

231
00:09:25,041 --> 00:09:26,875
B-O-R-ing.

232
00:09:26,875 --> 00:09:28,583
I bet Lloyd and Sora and them

233
00:09:28,583 --> 00:09:30,083
are having none of the borings.

234
00:09:30,083 --> 00:09:31,083
[groaning]

235
00:09:31,083 --> 00:09:32,000
You wanna blow up some rocks?

236
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,208
[groaning] Ugh.

237
00:09:34,458 --> 00:09:37,958
You never have to ask
such things.

238
00:09:37,958 --> 00:09:39,291
[♪♪♪]

239
00:09:39,291 --> 00:09:40,916
[laughing]

240
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:44,291
[screeching]

241
00:09:44,291 --> 00:09:46,291
Ooh!

242
00:09:46,291 --> 00:09:48,708
It's for me, it's for me!

243
00:09:48,708 --> 00:09:51,541
Ooh, I wonder who it's from.

244
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:54,666
Aw...

245
00:09:54,666 --> 00:09:55,916
look at that.

246
00:09:55,916 --> 00:09:57,333
Roby!

247
00:09:58,791 --> 00:10:00,416
Go away!

248
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:02,166
Aw, cute.

249
00:10:02,166 --> 00:10:04,083
He wants me to send a selfie!

250
00:10:10,083 --> 00:10:11,666
[Kai] Photobomb!

251
00:10:11,666 --> 00:10:13,916
Take this to Roby.

252
00:10:13,916 --> 00:10:15,333
'Kay, thanks!

253
00:10:16,958 --> 00:10:17,958
Wait.

254
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:19,416
Should I have waited
a few minutes

255
00:10:19,416 --> 00:10:20,791
before sending that?

256
00:10:20,791 --> 00:10:22,916
Am I gonna seem too needy?

257
00:10:22,916 --> 00:10:24,750
Unsend! Unsend!

258
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:26,791
Will you two please focus?

259
00:10:26,791 --> 00:10:29,500
Am I the only one that cares
about finding Jay?

260
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,375
[sighing] You're right, Nya.

261
00:10:31,375 --> 00:10:33,000
I haven't been much help.

262
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,583
[scoffing] You really haven't.

263
00:10:34,583 --> 00:10:35,666
It's just...

264
00:10:35,666 --> 00:10:37,083
I don't know what to do,

265
00:10:37,083 --> 00:10:38,458
and when I don't know
what to do,

266
00:10:38,458 --> 00:10:40,833
I hit rocks with fire.

267
00:10:40,833 --> 00:10:42,166
Hard relate.

268
00:10:42,166 --> 00:10:43,583
[sighing]

269
00:10:43,583 --> 00:10:44,750
I get it.

270
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,916
This whole thing
is overwhelming,

271
00:10:46,916 --> 00:10:48,458
but we need to focus

272
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:50,041
and come up with a plan.

273
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:52,166
If we don't,

274
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:53,875
Jay could be lost forever.

275
00:10:57,625 --> 00:10:59,333
[grunting]

276
00:10:59,333 --> 00:11:00,750
Huh?

277
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:02,500
[groaning] Uh...

278
00:11:11,666 --> 00:11:12,500
Oh, you're awake!

279
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,625
Here, this will help your arm.

280
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:15,583
[wincing]

281
00:11:15,583 --> 00:11:18,333
...but not your nose.
My apologies.

282
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:19,833
[wincing]

283
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:22,541
[sighing] Thanks.

284
00:11:22,541 --> 00:11:25,291
So... who are you?

285
00:11:25,291 --> 00:11:26,833
Where am I?

286
00:11:26,833 --> 00:11:28,000
What happened?

287
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,833
My name is Tyr,
head of the Dragonian tribe,

288
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,541
and you're in our village.

289
00:11:32,541 --> 00:11:34,166
Some of us found you
in the river,

290
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:35,541
and I gotta admit,

291
00:11:35,541 --> 00:11:36,708
they're a little disappointed

292
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:38,958
that you weren't a tasty fish.

293
00:11:38,958 --> 00:11:40,875
Sorry for not being a fish.

294
00:11:40,875 --> 00:11:43,000
But what about my friends?

295
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,041
[snoring]

296
00:11:44,041 --> 00:11:45,958
They'll be fine
as soon as they wake.

297
00:11:45,958 --> 00:11:48,666
But here, you must be hungry.

298
00:11:50,208 --> 00:11:51,708
[slurping]

299
00:11:53,041 --> 00:11:55,166
[♪♪♪]

300
00:11:56,875 --> 00:11:58,583
[crowd bustling and laughing]

301
00:12:08,416 --> 00:12:11,083
[Sora] Wow, these designs
are beautiful.

302
00:12:11,083 --> 00:12:13,083
It's an old Oni design.

303
00:12:13,083 --> 00:12:14,083
What's an Oni?

304
00:12:14,083 --> 00:12:16,625
[sudden silence]

305
00:12:16,625 --> 00:12:18,666
Did I say something wrong?

306
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:19,666
[gasping]

307
00:12:19,666 --> 00:12:21,625
[quietly]
The Oni were this race

308
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:23,083
of super-evil demons

309
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:26,250
at war with the dragons
a long time ago, and--

310
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:27,583
-Why?
-Why what?

311
00:12:27,583 --> 00:12:29,375
Why were they at war
with the dragons?

312
00:12:29,375 --> 00:12:31,500
Because of...

313
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,875
evil reasons.

314
00:12:32,875 --> 00:12:34,458
So you don't know?

315
00:12:34,458 --> 00:12:36,875
The Oni and Dragons
were part of the First Realm,

316
00:12:36,875 --> 00:12:38,125
and were at war

317
00:12:38,125 --> 00:12:40,750
even before the First
Spinjitzu Master was born.

318
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:43,583
And he was like
a relative of yours, right?

319
00:12:43,583 --> 00:12:44,750
Right.

320
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:46,875
He originally came from
the Realm of the Oni

321
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:48,125
and the dragons, too.

322
00:12:48,125 --> 00:12:50,416
That's exactly
what I was gonna say.

323
00:12:50,416 --> 00:12:52,083
The First Realm?

324
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:53,750
But where was that?

325
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:56,166
Looks like...

326
00:12:56,166 --> 00:12:58,125
we're in it now.

327
00:12:58,125 --> 00:13:00,000
This must be where
the First Realm appeared

328
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,333
during the Merge,

329
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:03,083
but only dragons
and these Dragonians

330
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:04,291
are left here now.

331
00:13:04,291 --> 00:13:05,875
And they're on our side.

332
00:13:06,833 --> 00:13:07,833
Man...

333
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:10,166
if I ever saw
one of those evil Oni...

334
00:13:10,166 --> 00:13:11,166
[shuddering]

335
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:13,500
I wonder if anyone
has seen Arin.

336
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,500
Let's ask Tyr.

337
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,958
Actually,

338
00:13:15,958 --> 00:13:18,291
you know who would know?

339
00:13:18,291 --> 00:13:19,625
Them.

340
00:13:19,625 --> 00:13:22,583
Old ladies know everything
that happens in a village.

341
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:29,666
Ooh, hi there, sweet pea,
what's good?

342
00:13:29,666 --> 00:13:31,083
We're looking for my friend.

343
00:13:31,083 --> 00:13:32,125
Have you seen him?

344
00:13:32,125 --> 00:13:33,291
Maybe,

345
00:13:33,291 --> 00:13:35,250
but we're going to need
more information

346
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:36,916
than "my friend."

347
00:13:36,916 --> 00:13:38,083
We don't know your life.

348
00:13:38,083 --> 00:13:39,375
Oh, yeah.

349
00:13:39,375 --> 00:13:40,416
His name is Arin.

350
00:13:41,625 --> 00:13:42,750
He's this high.

351
00:13:43,625 --> 00:13:45,833
Is probably wearing a hood?

352
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:47,875
With horns on it!

353
00:13:47,875 --> 00:13:50,166
Ooh, that guy!

354
00:13:50,166 --> 00:13:53,125
Why didn't you say "horns"
first?

355
00:13:53,125 --> 00:13:54,250
So you know where he is?

356
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,208
Yes!

357
00:13:55,208 --> 00:13:57,125
Well, no.

358
00:13:57,125 --> 00:13:58,041
We did.

359
00:13:58,041 --> 00:13:59,750
But he looked kinda Oni-like,

360
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,166
what with the horns and all,

361
00:14:01,166 --> 00:14:02,833
so we chased him away.

362
00:14:02,833 --> 00:14:05,041
Right toward the South Woods.

363
00:14:05,041 --> 00:14:06,041
He was alone?

364
00:14:06,041 --> 00:14:08,250
Well, he wasn't
with anyone else

365
00:14:08,250 --> 00:14:09,333
when we saw him,

366
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:12,000
but we don't know
his relationship status,

367
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,250
if that's what you're asking.

368
00:14:14,250 --> 00:14:17,375
Well, the good news is
he's alive.

369
00:14:17,375 --> 00:14:18,250
Yes!

370
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:20,291
Well, no.

371
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:21,333
He was.

372
00:14:21,333 --> 00:14:23,208
But he's probably dead now.

373
00:14:23,208 --> 00:14:24,583
Cyclops.

374
00:14:24,583 --> 00:14:25,833
Cyclops...

375
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:26,916
Cyclops?

376
00:14:26,916 --> 00:14:28,625
[together] Cyclops.

377
00:14:28,625 --> 00:14:30,208
There've been cyclops sightings

378
00:14:30,208 --> 00:14:32,625
from some other realm
in the South Woods.

379
00:14:32,625 --> 00:14:33,666
Yup.

380
00:14:33,666 --> 00:14:35,708
We sent
a Dragonian Hunting Party

381
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,208
out to look into it, but...

382
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:38,875
But...

383
00:14:38,875 --> 00:14:40,375
But?

384
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:42,083
[together]
They never came back.

385
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:44,958
Okay...

386
00:14:44,958 --> 00:14:47,083
Arin is a Ninja.

387
00:14:47,083 --> 00:14:48,583
He could survive.

388
00:14:48,583 --> 00:14:49,583
Yeah.

389
00:14:49,583 --> 00:14:51,541
Even if there were a--

390
00:14:51,541 --> 00:14:53,041
[together] Cyclops.

391
00:14:53,041 --> 00:14:55,875
--that doesn't mean
Arin isn't still alive.

392
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:58,916
So, into the South Woods we go.

393
00:15:04,666 --> 00:15:07,291
[forest birds calling]

394
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:13,875
[sniffing]

395
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,166
Got his scent, Riyu?

396
00:15:16,166 --> 00:15:17,208
[sniffing]

397
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:18,083
[grumbling affirmatively]

398
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,125
-Yes!
-Yeah!

399
00:15:19,125 --> 00:15:20,125
[sniffing]

400
00:15:20,125 --> 00:15:21,500
[growling]

401
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,583
Who else you smelling? Ras?

402
00:15:23,583 --> 00:15:24,625
The Forbidden Five?

403
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:31,250
[all] Whoa...

404
00:15:33,375 --> 00:15:35,500
What is this place?

405
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,708
It looks like someone's home.

406
00:15:37,708 --> 00:15:39,791
Kinda cozy, actually.

407
00:15:39,791 --> 00:15:41,375
[muffled cries]

408
00:15:41,375 --> 00:15:42,750
You hear that?

409
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,791
It's coming from...

410
00:15:44,791 --> 00:15:45,833
the ground?

411
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:47,125
[muffled voices crying out]

412
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:48,583
I think it's coming
from under that rock!

413
00:15:48,583 --> 00:15:49,708
Give me a hand.

414
00:15:51,333 --> 00:15:53,250
[grunting with effort]

415
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:54,666
Push with your knees,
not your back!

416
00:15:54,666 --> 00:15:55,791
I know!

417
00:15:55,791 --> 00:15:58,708
This isn't my first
giant rock, Frak!

418
00:16:00,875 --> 00:16:02,166
[stone grinding]

419
00:16:02,166 --> 00:16:03,458
It's the hunting party!

420
00:16:03,458 --> 00:16:04,458
They're still alive!

421
00:16:04,458 --> 00:16:05,375
Kinda!

422
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:06,875
Get us out of here!

423
00:16:06,875 --> 00:16:07,875
[grunting]

424
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:10,833
Take my hand!

425
00:16:12,125 --> 00:16:14,500
[heavy thudding]

426
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,458
I don't wanna turn around...

427
00:16:16,458 --> 00:16:18,083
[footsteps thumping]

428
00:16:18,916 --> 00:16:20,750
[roaring]

429
00:16:20,750 --> 00:16:23,250
I am PowerLid!

430
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:25,458
The ultimate cyclops!

431
00:16:25,458 --> 00:16:26,458
[roaring]

432
00:16:27,666 --> 00:16:29,291
Also known as

433
00:16:29,291 --> 00:16:32,416
the Ultimate Object
of Admiration!

434
00:16:32,416 --> 00:16:35,708
[whispering] I don't think
that last part is true.

435
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:37,958
[PowerLid roaring]

436
00:16:37,958 --> 00:16:39,750
Wait here
while we deal with this guy.

437
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:42,416
Ugh, would you?
He's super annoying.

438
00:16:42,416 --> 00:16:43,333
[roaring]

439
00:16:45,791 --> 00:16:47,041
H'yah!

440
00:16:47,041 --> 00:16:49,291
He's annoying, but also strong.

441
00:16:52,875 --> 00:16:55,208
Lloyd, your Spinjitzu!

442
00:16:55,208 --> 00:16:57,583
Yeah, feels weird.

443
00:16:57,583 --> 00:16:59,041
[PowerLid roaring]

444
00:17:02,833 --> 00:17:04,916
Eat rocks, Ninjerks!

445
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:07,458
Ha!

446
00:17:07,458 --> 00:17:09,000
Hit me all you want.

447
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,416
PowerLid can't feel a thing!

448
00:17:11,416 --> 00:17:13,791
Stub my toe, no pain!

449
00:17:13,791 --> 00:17:15,000
Bonk my head?

450
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:15,875
Nothing!

451
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:19,083
I can't even feel love.

452
00:17:19,083 --> 00:17:22,666
But PowerLid is not ready
to expose himself emotionally.

453
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:23,666
[sniffling]

454
00:17:23,666 --> 00:17:24,708
Eat more rocks!

455
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:29,333
Wait, don't move!

456
00:17:29,333 --> 00:17:32,500
Cyclopses don't perceive depth
with just one eye.

457
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,541
He can't separate us
from our surroundings

458
00:17:34,541 --> 00:17:35,875
as long as we don't move!

459
00:17:35,875 --> 00:17:36,875
[stomping]

460
00:17:36,875 --> 00:17:37,875
[sniffing]

461
00:17:37,875 --> 00:17:39,291
Ninja?

462
00:17:39,291 --> 00:17:40,750
Where you go?

463
00:17:43,083 --> 00:17:45,541
Just kidding,
PowerLid can see you!

464
00:17:45,541 --> 00:17:46,500
[gasping]

465
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,708
That's a stupid

466
00:17:47,708 --> 00:17:49,916
and harmful Cyclops stereotype!

467
00:17:49,916 --> 00:17:51,458
[stomping]

468
00:17:51,458 --> 00:17:52,708
You little know-it-all!

469
00:17:52,708 --> 00:17:54,083
You almost got us killed!

470
00:17:55,250 --> 00:17:56,541
[panting]

471
00:17:57,541 --> 00:17:58,833
[roaring]

472
00:17:58,833 --> 00:17:59,750
[grunting with effort]

473
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:00,708
[yelping]

474
00:18:00,708 --> 00:18:01,666
H'yah!

475
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:03,791
Nothing is working!

476
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:06,166
[grunting and gasping]

477
00:18:07,166 --> 00:18:09,750
Run from PowerLid!

478
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:13,083
The Ultimate Object
of Admiration!

479
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:19,958
Is that all you got?

480
00:18:19,958 --> 00:18:22,458
That rock was pretty heavy.

481
00:18:22,458 --> 00:18:24,375
Denser than it looked, maybe.

482
00:18:24,375 --> 00:18:27,541
Probably peridotite, or gabbro.

483
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:29,458
Just saying, it looked tiny...

484
00:18:29,458 --> 00:18:30,666
for someone who calls himself

485
00:18:30,666 --> 00:18:32,916
the Ultimate Object
of Admiration.

486
00:18:32,916 --> 00:18:35,208
I can pick up bigger!

487
00:18:35,208 --> 00:18:36,500
Watch! [roaring]

488
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,500
Ha!

489
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,083
Nice aim, Tiny Rocks.

490
00:18:40,083 --> 00:18:41,708
[PowerLid grunting] H'yah!

491
00:18:41,708 --> 00:18:42,916
[Sora] Nope! [laughing]

492
00:18:44,541 --> 00:18:46,875
Stop moving, little Ninja!

493
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:47,708
Tell you what,

494
00:18:47,708 --> 00:18:49,166
I'll stop moving

495
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:51,875
if you can pick up that rock
and throw it at me.

496
00:18:51,875 --> 00:18:53,000
Promise?

497
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,750
That rock not that heavy, even!

498
00:18:55,750 --> 00:18:57,125
Watch PowerLid.

499
00:18:57,125 --> 00:19:00,083
PowerLid is swole!

500
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:03,958
[grunting]

501
00:19:03,958 --> 00:19:05,000
[groaning]

502
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
PowerLid getting tired.

503
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,500
Maybe not enough protein today.

504
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,000
Doesn't count unless
you lift it over your head.

505
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
It count!

506
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Nope!

507
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,791
[grunting]

508
00:19:17,791 --> 00:19:19,000
[straining]

509
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Ha!

510
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,083
[groaning]

511
00:19:22,083 --> 00:19:24,083
Oof!

512
00:19:24,083 --> 00:19:25,333
[groaning]

513
00:19:25,333 --> 00:19:27,041
Yeah!
[laughing in triumph]

514
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:29,208
Quick thinking, Sora.

515
00:19:29,208 --> 00:19:30,458
Nice.

516
00:19:30,458 --> 00:19:31,458
Yeah.

517
00:19:31,458 --> 00:19:33,916
Now let's get-- going?

518
00:19:35,791 --> 00:19:37,375
Who are you?

519
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,333
What was that all about?

520
00:19:45,333 --> 00:19:47,291
[grunting and snoring]

521
00:19:47,291 --> 00:19:49,583
[murmuring sleepily]
Object of Admiration...

522
00:19:49,583 --> 00:19:51,041
[snoring]

523
00:19:51,041 --> 00:19:52,541
[♪♪♪]

524
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:57,375
Any chance you've seen
my friend, Arin?

525
00:19:57,375 --> 00:19:59,750
He was wearing a hood
with horns, and--

526
00:19:59,750 --> 00:20:01,166
Dragging someone on a sled?

527
00:20:01,166 --> 00:20:02,083
Maybe?

528
00:20:02,083 --> 00:20:04,041
When did you see him?
Was he okay?

529
00:20:04,041 --> 00:20:05,708
Mm, no idea.

530
00:20:05,708 --> 00:20:08,833
We were kinda busy
being stuck in a cyclops hole,

531
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:11,291
but I think he went that way.

532
00:20:12,458 --> 00:20:13,458
Great!

533
00:20:13,458 --> 00:20:14,416
He's headed South.

534
00:20:14,416 --> 00:20:15,416
Come on--

535
00:20:15,416 --> 00:20:16,666
What now?

536
00:20:16,666 --> 00:20:18,791
Wanna serpent-splain
"South" to me?

537
00:20:18,791 --> 00:20:20,416
No! I...

538
00:20:20,416 --> 00:20:21,875
I want to apologize.

539
00:20:21,875 --> 00:20:22,875
Oh.

540
00:20:22,875 --> 00:20:23,958
I...

541
00:20:23,958 --> 00:20:27,041
I know I could have
gotten us all killed.

542
00:20:27,041 --> 00:20:30,375
I was trying to show you
I'm not just Ras's stooge.

543
00:20:30,375 --> 00:20:32,875
We know that. Kinda.

544
00:20:32,875 --> 00:20:34,208
Maybe I could've stopped Arin

545
00:20:34,208 --> 00:20:35,125
from going with Ras

546
00:20:35,125 --> 00:20:36,958
if I had just talked to him.

547
00:20:36,958 --> 00:20:38,250
It's not your fault.

548
00:20:38,250 --> 00:20:39,625
You really believe that?

549
00:20:39,625 --> 00:20:40,833
Yeah,

550
00:20:40,833 --> 00:20:41,916
because...

551
00:20:41,916 --> 00:20:44,708
I think it's my fault.

552
00:20:44,708 --> 00:20:47,291
Arin and I weren't talking
when he left.

553
00:20:47,291 --> 00:20:49,166
He was my first friend.

554
00:20:49,166 --> 00:20:50,583
Did you know that?

555
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:52,083
I... didn't.

556
00:20:52,083 --> 00:20:53,958
Yeah, well,

557
00:20:53,958 --> 00:20:56,416
I'm not very good at
making friends.

558
00:20:56,416 --> 00:20:59,083
So, you two ready or what?

559
00:20:59,083 --> 00:21:00,291
-Yes.
-Of course.

560
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:05,583
[Ras groaning and wheezing]

561
00:21:05,583 --> 00:21:06,583
We should stop soon,

562
00:21:06,583 --> 00:21:07,583
eat a bit,

563
00:21:07,583 --> 00:21:08,791
maybe put on some sunscreen.

564
00:21:08,791 --> 00:21:09,958
[wheezing]

565
00:21:09,958 --> 00:21:10,875
No!

566
00:21:10,875 --> 00:21:12,291
Keep moving!

567
00:21:12,291 --> 00:21:14,458
You can't run from the sun.

568
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:15,708
It'll only take a minute.

569
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:16,791
[growling]

570
00:21:16,791 --> 00:21:19,500
I demand we go faster!

571
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,250
You think
I don't want to find my parents

572
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:22,708
as fast as we can?

573
00:21:22,708 --> 00:21:24,500
But we can't be stupid
out here.

574
00:21:25,541 --> 00:21:27,666
I promised we'd find
your parents,

575
00:21:27,666 --> 00:21:29,666
and I always keep my word!

576
00:21:29,666 --> 00:21:30,916
[wheezing]

577
00:21:30,916 --> 00:21:33,500
But my injuries are grave.

578
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,791
I must heal.

579
00:21:34,791 --> 00:21:36,291
Of course.

580
00:21:36,291 --> 00:21:37,541
To do that,

581
00:21:37,541 --> 00:21:40,208
there's only one place
we must go...

582
00:21:41,541 --> 00:21:45,000
The Spectral Lands.

583
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

